Subject: [PATCH 493/496] [DS4.1] TileLang is the model's only kernel family:
 the B12X family goes

Serving selects TileLang for the whole model (VLLM_DS41_KERNEL_BACKEND,
--attention-backend TILELANG, --linear-backend/--moe-backend tilelang), so
the B12X family's model code never runs. It goes:

- kernels.py: every component is TileLang's (no uses_tilelang(); the
  always-on MOE_FP32_COMBINE and SHARED_SWIGLU_FP32 switches go with it);
- b12x_layers.py, nvidia/b12x_vision.py and nvidia/b12x_attention.py;
- attention.py: the helper plans and _AttentionHelpers, the B12X sparse MLA,
  indexer and WO plans, preparation units and calls, B12X RoPE, cache writes,
  index-weight scaling and the WO pack/projection (_o_proj is TileLang's,
  without the positions and is_prefill it no longer reads);
- compressor.py: the B12X projection plans, compression plan and primer;
- engram: the B12X hash (its metadata kernel, bindings and hash plans) and the
  B12X Engram mix (its plans, boolean masks and pack_columns); the hash and
  gate take the step's token ids, as TileLang's do;
- dspark.py: _ContextKVProjection (TileLangBlock32Rows is the projection);
- model.py, dspark.py: the B12X layer registry and mHC providers, which only
  B12xMHC's custom ops read;
- sparse_mla.py: the builder's Triton dispatch (the kernels go next).

Kept, because serving still reaches them: the b12x Engram geometry, token map
and caps, and the B12X lookup of resident (device/RAM) Engram tables; the
B12X checkpoint loader; the generic B12X preparation pass (it binds the
TileLang vocabulary heads); the shared V4.1 cache layout classes
(DeepseekV41B12x*), whose names are upstream's.

Tests: B12X-only DS4.1 tests go (WO/indexer/helper plans, B12X RMSNorm,
B12X vision, the B12X workspace file, B12X DS4.1 linear, mHC and embedding
tests in test_b12x_linear.py, the B12X DSpark context graph test, the
compressor projection/mHC/context projection preparation tests). Ported to
TileLang: the compressor's rejection/reorder/page-boundary and high-offset
tests, the Engram model tests (token ids for the gate), the SP Engram gate
test, the attention staging tests; moved: the builder's graph-refresh and the
custom op functionalization tests. The TileLang vision test keeps its torch
models of the arithmetic and FP64 references (fixed bounds) without B12X's
kernels, and its B12X benchmark goes.
